"""Editorial question designs for fictional geography and short-form screen work."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


FICTIONAL_GEOGRAPHY = """history_origins|The First Map of a Fictional Place|Which documented sketch or text established a setting's geography?|Date the source and distinguish early from final versions.
famous_examples|A Literary Map Put to Work|How does a named map guide or complicate a story's journey?|Compare map, text, edition, and actual route.
hidden_stories|Who Drew the World?|Which cartographer, illustrator, or designer shaped a familiar fictional place?|Check credits, archival drafts, and publisher records.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Fictional Map|What do scale, orientation, legend, and omissions allow a reader to infer?|Use one identified map and its accompanying text.
advanced_concepts|Geography as Narrative Constraint|How do distance, terrain, and borders shape character options?|Trace a bounded route and decision in the work.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unmapped Region|Does the text leave a place intentionally vague or contradict its map?|Compare versions and state unresolved gaps.
technology_innovation|A Navigable Fictional Map|What changes when an audience can explore rather than view a fixed map?|Test a released interactive version and its limits.
people_personalities|A Mapmaker's Revision|What evidence explains a changed coastline, border, or place name?|Use dated drafts and attributed notes.
major_events|A New Edition Redraws the World|Which publication or adaptation changed spatial information?|Compare authorized versions and reader access.
how_it_works|Plotting a Journey|Can the sequence of travel fit the geography the work establishes?|Trace locations, times, and stated transport.
rise_fall|A Location Removed from Canon|Which version dropped or relocated a fictional site?|Check publication and production chronology.
then_vs_now|One World across Two Maps|Which places, labels, or boundaries changed between editions?|Compare identified maps at similar scale.
future_developments|An Expanding Fictional Atlas|Which planned location has documented constraints from existing works?|Date plans and avoid treating proposals as released canon.
myths_vs_facts|A Map Is the Whole World?|What does a map omit despite appearing complete?|Check text, map purpose, scale, and perspective.
documentary_stories|Making a Fictional Map|How did a route or settlement move from sketch to release?|Follow drafts, editorial decisions, and credits.
creative_brief|What the Map Must Explain|Which story action required a particular spatial relationship?|Compare brief, sketch, and final scene.
materials_and_tools|Sketches, Grids, and Place Lists|What do working maps reveal about setting design?|Identify author, version, scale, and intended use.
process_breakdown|Revising a Route|Which travel inconsistency or story need prompted a map change?|Compare drafts and resulting narrative.
composition_choice|Map as Storytelling Image|How do labels and visual hierarchy direct attention?|Analyze one map and its narrative moment.
collaborative_authorship|Map and Text Made Together|How did writer, illustrator, editor, and game designer shape a geography?|Use credits and asset history.
adaptation_across_media|A Map Becomes a Screen Place|Which distances and borders survive an adaptation?|Compare source map, production design, and released scenes.
audience_reception|Readers Navigate the Setting|What documented confusion or interpretation concerns a route?|Use situated feedback and version details.
cultural_context|Real Places behind Imaginary Ones|Which named landscape or mapping tradition influenced the fiction?|Attribute sources without equating fiction to a real community.
preservation_restoration|A Map's Surviving Versions|What do archived drafts reveal that a printed map cannot?|Record provenance and missing stages.
rights_and_attribution|Rights to a Fictional Map|Who authored a particular image and who controls its reuse?|Separate underlying story world, map artwork, and license.
style_comparison|Two Maps of One Setting|How do different projections or purposes change apparent geography?|Compare scale, orientation, and edition.
creative_failure|A Place Cut from the Map|What documented constraint removed a location?|Use draft and editorial evidence, not speculative intent.
field_internal_rules|A Route within the Rules|Do distances and travel methods stay consistent?|Track time, speed, obstacles, and exceptions.
field_character_motivation|Why Travel There?|Do a character's destination and route follow their goals and knowledge?|Compare alternatives visible on the map.
field_narrative_pacing|Distance between Scenes|Does travel time support the sequence of events?|Map elapsed time and omitted travel.
field_setting_logic|Water, Borders, and Supply|Can settlements and journeys work under the work's stated geography?|Test only consequences established or invited by the text.
field_genre_expectations|A Map Promises Adventure|Which route or blank space creates a genre expectation?|Compare image, narrative, and situated reception.
"""

WEB_SERIES = """history_origins|A Series Born for the Web|Which distribution constraint shaped an early web-first series?|Compare dated release, format, and production records.
famous_examples|An Episode That Defines a Series|How does one episode establish recurring premise and viewer expectations?|Analyze episode, release order, and stated format.
hidden_stories|Small-Team Series Labor|Whose writing, camera, editing, moderation, or promotion sustained a season?|Check credits, production logs, and interviews.
beginner_explainers|What Makes an Episode Work Alone?|What must a new viewer learn in a short installment?|Map setup, prior context, and payoff in one episode.
advanced_concepts|Serial Continuity Online|How does a series balance episode closure with season arcs?|Track reveals and unresolved threads across identified releases.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Missing or Recut Episode|Which version survives and what is uncertain about the original upload?|Compare archive captures, metadata, and creator records.
technology_innovation|Platform Feature as Story Device|Did comments, links, or release tools alter an episode's design?|Document actual platform affordances and decisions.
people_personalities|A Showrunner's Revision|Which documented feedback changed a later episode?|Compare scripts, release chronology, and attributed account.
major_events|A Web Series Changes Platform|What changed in access, format, or ownership after a move?|Use dated platform terms and release records.
how_it_works|From Script to Upload|Which steps produce and publish one episode?|Trace approval, shoot, edit, captions, metadata, and version.
rise_fall|A Series Pauses or Ends|What documented factors explain an interrupted release schedule?|Use production statements and dates; avoid guessing finances.
then_vs_now|A Web Episode across Versions|What changed between original post, reupload, and compilation?|Compare identifiable files and release context.
future_developments|A Planned Next Season|What resources and rights would a documented renewal require?|Treat announcements as conditional until release.
myths_vs_facts|Views Equal a Fanbase?|What can public platform metrics establish about actual viewers?|Distinguish impressions, plays, completion, and unique audience.
documentary_stories|Making an Online Season|How did a team schedule, produce, and release consecutive episodes?|Follow dated scripts, shoots, and uploads.
creative_brief|The Series Format Promise|What episode length, tone, and release rhythm did a brief set?|Compare plan with published season.
materials_and_tools|Lean Series Production|Which camera, sound, and edit choices met a real budget or schedule?|Use actual equipment and production records.
process_breakdown|An Episode's Revision Trail|How did a scene change between script, shoot, and upload?|Compare dated artifacts and final version.
composition_choice|Framing for the Intended Screen|What image details remain legible at the designed viewing size?|Test released format and shot scale.
collaborative_authorship|Credits across Episodes|How did writing and craft roles vary through a season?|Compare episode credits and contracts where applicable.
adaptation_across_media|A Series Becomes a Feature|What story information changes when episodes are compiled?|Compare release order, bridging scenes, and feature cut.
audience_reception|Comments as Evidence|What can a visible comment sample show about response?|Account for moderation, self-selection, and platform change.
cultural_context|A Series for a Specific Community|Which language or local references shape its premise?|Use creator and audience sources, not generalizations.
preservation_restoration|Archiving a Web Series|What files, captions, metadata, and links survive after a platform change?|Record versions and missing context.
rights_and_attribution|Online Release Rights|Who may reuse music, clips, performances, and scripts in a web episode?|Check actual licenses and applicable credit rules.
style_comparison|Two Web-First Formats|How do release cadence and episode length change a similar premise?|Compare documented series and viewer pathways.
creative_failure|An Episode Reworked after Release|What documented issue prompted a reupload or correction?|Compare versions and creator notice.
field_shot_design|The Vertical or Horizontal Shot|How did intended aspect ratio shape staging?|Compare shot plans with released crops.
field_production_workflow|Producing a Season in Batches|Which handoffs affect continuity and delivery?|Trace schedule, asset reuse, and revision control.
field_sound_choices|Sound for Small Speakers|Which dialogue and mix choices remain intelligible on intended devices?|Compare master, captions, and playback tests.
field_editing_rhythm|An Online Episode's Opening|How quickly does it establish context without losing clarity?|Map cut timing and necessary information.
field_distribution_format|One Episode on Several Platforms|What changes in crop, caption, metadata, or rights across outlets?|Compare actual published versions and terms.
"""

SHORT_FILMS = """history_origins|A Short Film in Its Program|Which exhibition or production context shaped one short work?|Use dated program, print, and production records.
famous_examples|A Short's Central Choice|How does a named film build a complete turn within its runtime?|Analyze timecoded setup, change, and ending.
hidden_stories|Crew behind a Short|Whose craft made a low-budget or student film possible?|Check credits, call sheets, and participant accounts.
beginner_explainers|A Short Film's Focus|Which information can be established with a small number of scenes?|Map character, action, and consequence in one film.
advanced_concepts|Compression without Confusion|How does a short use ellipsis or visual inference to omit exposition?|Compare what is shown, implied, and left ambiguous.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Lost Short or Alternate Cut|Which version or release history remains unverified?|Check archive catalogs, festival programs, and masters.
technology_innovation|A Tool Opens Short-Film Production|Which actual production barrier did a new tool lower?|Compare one film's workflow, cost, and distribution evidence.
people_personalities|A Short-Film Maker's Revision|Why did a filmmaker change a scene or ending?|Use dated drafts, edits, and attributed account.
major_events|A Short Reaches a New Audience|What followed a particular festival, broadcast, or online release?|Trace distribution and documented response; avoid causal inflation.
how_it_works|One Short from Brief to Screening|What steps turned a small story into a finished film?|Follow script, shoot, edit, sound, delivery, and rights.
rise_fall|An Early Short Reassessed|How did interpretation of a filmmaker's early work change?|Compare dated criticism and access to the film.
then_vs_now|A Short across Formats|How does a cinema screening differ from a later online version?|Compare master, framing, sound, and viewing context.
future_developments|A Short as a Proof of Concept|What can a finished short demonstrate about a proposed longer work?|Separate documented production capacity from promised financing.
myths_vs_facts|Short Means Simple?|Which production tasks remain even when runtime is brief?|Use a real short's schedule, credits, and deliverables.
documentary_stories|The Making of a Short|How did constraints shape one scene from first draft to final mix?|Follow versioned artifacts and crew accounts.
creative_brief|The One Essential Turn|What change did a short's brief ask the audience to follow?|Compare pitch, script, and final ending.
materials_and_tools|A Minimal Production Kit|Which tools served the short's actual visual and sound needs?|Specify setup and limits without prescribing universal gear.
process_breakdown|Cutting to Runtime|Which scenes or beats were removed, and what story function survived?|Compare rough and final cuts with timing.
composition_choice|An Image Carries a Plot Beat|Which framed action replaces spoken explanation?|Analyze a bounded shot and its surrounding sequence.
collaborative_authorship|Credits on a Small Crew|How did combined roles affect creative decisions and attribution?|Use credits, agreements, and participant records.
adaptation_across_media|A Short from a Written Source|Which source event became the film's central action?|Compare rights, script, and released work.
audience_reception|A Short in Different Programs|How did screening context affect documented interpretation?|Compare program notes, reviews, and audience evidence.
cultural_context|A Local Short's Setting|Which place and community details matter to its story?|Use production and local sources without generalizing.
preservation_restoration|Saving a Short Film|Which camera originals, project files, captions, and masters survive?|Inventory assets and version history.
rights_and_attribution|Clearing a Short for Release|Which music, image, location, and performer permissions matter?|Check actual production agreements and jurisdiction.
style_comparison|Two Short Endings|How do two films use final image or sound to reframe earlier action?|Compare matched runtimes and formal choices.
creative_failure|A Short Recut|What documented feedback or constraint prompted a new edit?|Use edit history rather than assume poor response.
field_shot_design|A Shot with More than One Job|How does framing establish place, character, and action efficiently?|Compare storyboard and final shot.
field_production_workflow|A One-Day Shoot Plan|Which schedule choices protect essential story beats?|Trace call sheet, setup changes, and actual footage.
field_sound_choices|Sound in a Small Story|What work do dialogue, room tone, and music perform within limited runtime?|Compare script cues and final mix.
field_editing_rhythm|Pacing a Short's Turn|Where does the film spend time before and after its central change?|Timecode shots and viewer information.
field_distribution_format|Festival and Online Versions|What deliverable, caption, aspect, or rights differences arise?|Compare documented submissions and published files.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("382", "382_fictional_geography", FICTIONAL_GEOGRAPHY,
                  "Fictional geography as maps, routes, distances, borders, and place relationships that shape a particular narrative world and its versions.",
                  "identified texts and maps, dated sketches, publisher and production records, archive catalogs, credited cartographers, and situated reader responses",
                  "State the fictional work and edition. Treat maps as versioned creative artifacts rather than complete or physically exact surveys; attribute real-world references.")
    revise_domain("383", "383_web_series", WEB_SERIES,
                  "Web series as episodic screen productions whose story, workflow, credit, versions, and audience access are shaped by online release.",
                  "identified episodes and upload dates, scripts, call sheets, platform metadata, credits and agreements, archive captures, and bounded audience evidence",
                  "Name platform, release, and version. Do not equate public view counters with unique viewers or assume one credit and rights system applies to every jurisdiction.")
    revise_domain("384", "384_short_films", SHORT_FILMS,
                  "Short films as complete moving-image works shaped by concentrated story design, production constraints, exhibition, delivery, and preservation.",
                  "identified films and cuts, scripts, production and sound records, festival or broadcast programs, rights documents, archives, and situated criticism",
                  "Name film, cut, runtime, and exhibition context. Avoid treating a short as automatically simple or a festival appearance as proof of broad impact.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
